# ============================================================================
# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# ============================================================================
# Format:  /from  /to  [status]
# 301 = permanent, 302 = temporary. Default is 302, so always state 301 for
# a permanent move or you will leak link equity.
#
# Order matters: the first match wins.
# ============================================================================

# --- Tidy URLs -------------------------------------------------------------
# Visitors and old links often guess these. Point them at the real page
# rather than letting them hit the 404.
/services/            /services.html          301
/service              /services.html          301
/locations/           /locations.html         301
/areas                /locations.html         301
/contact              /contact.html           301
/about                /about.html             301
/faq                  /faq.html               301
/quote                /contact.html           301
/estimate             /contact.html           301
/checklist            /guides/moving-checklist.html   301

# --- Index variants --------------------------------------------------------
/index                /                       301
/index.html           /                       301
/home                 /                       301

# --- Legal -----------------------------------------------------------------
/privacy              /privacy.html           301
/privacy-policy       /privacy.html           301
/terms                /terms.html             301
/terms-and-conditions /terms.html             301

# --- Development files, kept out of public view ----------------------------
# Everything in this folder is uploaded to Cloudflare Pages, including the
# authoring tools, the local dev server and the README. The README in
# particular is an internal handover document: it discusses which business
# claims are unverified and which copy still needs the owner's sign-off, and
# that is not something to leave on a public URL for a competitor to read.
#
# These rules send those paths to the 404 page. NOTE: on Cloudflare Pages a
# matching static asset can take precedence over a _redirects rule, so treat
# this as a guard rather than a guarantee — the definitive fix is to move the
# published site into its own subfolder and point the Pages "Root directory"
# at that. See README.md § Keeping development files off the public site.
/tools/*              /404.html               404
/README.md            /404.html               404
/serve.ps1            /404.html               404
/.env.example         /404.html               404

# --- Add a line here whenever you rename or remove a page. ----------------
# A removed page that returns 404 loses whatever ranking it had. A 301 to the
# closest equivalent keeps it. For example, after renaming a city page:
#   /locations/old-city.html   /locations/new-city.html   301
